#: src/ai/tools.md:3
msgid "Tools"
msgstr "工具"

#: src/ai/tools.md:5
msgid ""
"Zed's built-in agent has access to these tools for reading, searching, and "
"editing your codebase. These tools are used in the [Agent Panel](./agent-"
"panel.md) during conversations with AI agents."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:7
msgid ""
"You can configure permissions for tool actions, including situations where "
"they are automatically approved, automatically denied, or require your "
"confirmation on a case-by-case basis. See [Tool Permissions](./tool-"
"permissions.md) for the list of permission-gated tools and details."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:9
msgid ""
"To add custom tools beyond these built-in ones, see [MCP servers](./mcp.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:11
msgid "Read & Search Tools"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:13
msgid "`diagnostics`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:15
msgid ""
"Gets errors and warnings for either a specific file or the entire project, "
"useful after making edits to determine if further changes are needed. When a "
"path is provided, shows all diagnostics for that specific file. When no path "
"is provided, shows a summary of error and warning counts for all files in "
"the project."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:19
msgid ""
"**Example:** After editing `src/parser.rs`, call `diagnostics` with that "
"path to check for type errors immediately. After a larger refactor touching "
"many files, call it without a path to see a project-wide count of errors "
"before deciding what to fix next."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:21
msgid "`fetch`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:23
msgid ""
"Fetches a URL and returns the content as Markdown. Useful for providing docs "
"as context."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:25
msgid ""
"**Example:** Fetching a library's changelog page to check whether a breaking "
"API change was introduced in a recent version before writing integration "
"code."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:27
msgid "`find_path`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:29
msgid ""
"Quickly finds files by matching glob patterns (like \"\\*_/_.js\"), "
"returning matching file paths alphabetically."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:31
msgid "`grep`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:33
msgid ""
"Searches file contents across the project using regular expressions, "
"preferred for finding symbols in code without knowing exact file paths."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:35
msgid ""
"**Example:** To find every call site of a function before renaming it, "
"search for `parse_config\\(` — the regex matches the function name followed "
"by an opening parenthesis, filtering out comments or variable names that "
"happen to contain the string."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:37
msgid "`list_directory`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:39
msgid ""
"Lists files and directories in a given path, providing an overview of "
"filesystem contents."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:41
msgid "`now`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:43
msgid "Returns the current date and time."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:45
msgid "`open`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:47
msgid ""
"Opens a file or URL with the default application associated with it on the "
"user's operating system."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:49
msgid "`read_file`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:51
msgid ""
"Reads the content of a specified file in the project, allowing access to "
"file contents."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:53
msgid "`thinking`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:55
msgid ""
"Allows the Agent to work through problems, brainstorm ideas, or plan without "
"executing actions, useful for complex problem-solving."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:57
msgid "`web_search`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:59
msgid ""
"Searches the web for information, providing results with snippets and links "
"from relevant web pages, useful for accessing real-time information."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:61
msgid ""
"**Example:** Looking up whether a known bug in a dependency has been patched "
"in a recent release, or finding the current API signature for a third-party "
"library when the local docs are out of date."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:63
msgid "Edit Tools"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:65
msgid "`copy_path`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:67
msgid ""
"Copies a file or directory recursively in the project, more efficient than "
"manually reading and writing files when duplicating content."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:69
msgid "`create_directory`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:71
msgid ""
"Creates a new directory at the specified path within the project, creating "
"all necessary parent directories (similar to `mkdir -p`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:73
msgid "`delete_path`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:75
msgid ""
"Deletes a file or directory (including contents recursively) at the "
"specified path and confirms the deletion."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:77
msgid "`edit_file`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:79
msgid "Edits files by replacing specific text with new content."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:81
msgid ""
"**Example:** Updating a function signature — the agent identifies the exact "
"lines to replace and provides the updated version, leaving the surrounding "
"code untouched. For widespread renames, it pairs this with `grep` to find "
"every occurrence first."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:83
msgid "`move_path`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:85
msgid ""
"Moves or renames a file or directory in the project, performing a rename if "
"only the filename differs."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:87
msgid "`restore_file_from_disk`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:89
msgid ""
"Discards unsaved changes in open buffers by reloading file contents from "
"disk. Useful for resetting files to their on-disk state before retrying an "
"edit."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:91
msgid "`save_file`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:93
msgid ""
"Saves files that have unsaved changes. Used when files need to be saved "
"before further edits can be made."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:95
msgid "`terminal`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:97
msgid ""
"Executes shell commands and returns the combined output, creating a new "
"shell process for each invocation."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:99
msgid ""
"**Example:** After editing a Rust file, run `cargo test --package my_crate "
"2>&1 | tail -30` to confirm the changes don't break existing tests. Or run "
"`git diff --stat` to review which files have been modified before wrapping "
"up a task."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:101
msgid "Other Tools"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:103
msgid "`spawn_agent`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:105
msgid ""
"Spawns a subagent with its own context window to perform a delegated task. "
"Useful for running parallel investigations, completing self-contained tasks, "
"or performing research where only the outcome matters. Each subagent has "
"access to the same tools as the parent agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tools.md:107
msgid ""
"**Example:** While refactoring the authentication module, spawn a subagent "
"to investigate how session tokens are validated elsewhere in the codebase. "
"The parent agent continues its work and reviews the subagent's findings when "
"it completes — keeping both context windows focused on a single task."
msgstr ""
